# Does the change of representation across goals generalise?

Generated by `equiv2.py` (exploratory). For each ordered goal pair (A, B): maps from the A-written difference x2(A) − x1(A) to the B-written difference at the input of block 2, fitted on 12288 random same-step pairs of fit decisions (posteriors ≥ 0.5 apart); applied to the held-out A-equivalent, B-different pairs of `equiv.py` (test episodes; 451 (424–587) pairs per goal pair): x1(B) + T(Δ_A), logits read under B. Means over goal pairs, medians (min–max) over six models.

| vector added under B | B's decision to b2's | held-out R² for Δ_B |
|---|---|---|
| direct B-written difference Δ_B | 0.91 (0.89–0.96) | 1 |
| **linear map of Δ_A (ridge on differences)** | **0.86 (0.80–0.89)** | 0.95 (0.94–0.96) |
| MLP on differences | 0.89 (0.87–0.92) | 0.96 (0.96–0.97) |
| MLP from the A-written state to the B-written state | 0.91 (0.89–0.95) | 0.99 (0.99–0.99) |
| untransformed Δ_A | 0.33 (0.24–0.40) | 0.39 (0.37–0.51) |
| random, Δ_B's norm | 0.05 (0.02–0.06) | |

The linear map's vector added under A changes A's decision in 0.46 (0.37–0.53) of pairs.
